  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on which lottery is more left-skewed, i.e., assigns greater probability to favorable outcomes. In this context, favorable outcomes are those with no loss (0 Euros). Lottery B assigns 55% to 0€, Lottery A only 10%, so B is more left-skewed, and the reason would prefer B. The individual considers exactly this: the higher probability (55% vs. 10%) of avoiding a loss, and uses this as the main justification for choosing B. While they do not use the term 'skewness', they are clearly attending to the distribution of probability mass toward the more favorable outcome (no loss), which is the core of the skewness reason. Their deliberation aligns with the rule of preferring the lottery with more probability on favorable outcomes. Therefore, the individual is using reasoning that matches the decision reason, even if not labeled as such.",
